=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r1
diagnosis_text:
The FRR routing daemon is not running on r1, the campus border router. r1 has a
working default route to the ISP (203.0.113.1 via eth2), correct NAT/MASQUERADE
rules for all internal subnets, and a valid /etc/frr/frr.conf that configures
OSPF area 0 on the two core-facing links (10.0.0.32/30, 10.0.0.36/30) and
includes `default-information originate` to propagate a default route inward. The
problem is that none of this ever takes effect because the FRR process itself is
dead — no zebra, no ospfd, no frr processes appear in ps, and there is no runit
service directory (/etc/sv/frr) or sysvinit script (/etc/init.d/frr) to start it
at boot. As a result, r1 has never joined the OSPF topology: csw1's neighbor table
shows five peers (csw2, dswa1, dswa2, dswb1, dswb2) but r1 (router-id 10.0.0.76)
is absent. Because no default route is injected into OSPF, csw1, csw2, and all
four distribution switches have zero knowledge of how to reach external addresses.
PC1's traffic reaches dswa1 (its VLAN 10 gateway, 10.1.0.2), which immediately
returns ICMP Destination Network Unreachable. Every client on every internal subnet
is affected. Corrective fix: start FRR on r1 (`/usr/lib/frr/frrinit.sh start` or
equivalent) and add a persistent runit service so it survives reboots; once FRR
comes up and OSPF forms adjacency with csw1/csw2, the default route will propagate
automatically within seconds.
=== END ===
